From: x570d4i2t layer <root@x570d4i2t>
Date: Thu, 24 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ikvm_manager: survive a severed/lost video link

The host's aspeed-video signal on this board flaps (the BIOS drives an
unstable 800x600 output that periodically drops). When the V4L2 timings
query fails, Video::needsResize()/restart()/resize() throw an elog<>
exception. Upstream's Manager::run() wraps video.start() in try/catch but
NOT needsResize()/resize(), so the exception escapes run(), terminates the
process, and systemd restarts obmc-ikvm -- tearing down the client's KVM
session on every transient sever.

Wrap needsResize()/resize() in try/catch so the daemon survives a lost
signal and keeps serving (a stale/no-signal frame) until the signal
returns, keeping the KVM session connected. The sync handshake is kept
balanced: on a needsResize() failure we fall through to the no-resize
branch (setVideoDone(); waitServer()); on a resize() failure we still
setVideoDone() to release the paused server thread.
--- a/ikvm_manager.cpp
+++ b/ikvm_manager.cpp
@@ -40,11 +40,37 @@
             video.stop();
         }
 
-        if (video.needsResize())
+        bool resizeNeeded = false;
+        try
+        {
+            resizeNeeded = video.needsResize();
+        }
+        catch (const std::exception& e)
+        {
+            // A lost/severed video signal (e.g. host powered off, or the
+            // aspeed-video link flapping while the BIOS re-inits the display)
+            // makes the V4L2 timings query fail. Upstream lets that exception
+            // escape run(), which terminates the process; systemd then
+            // restarts obmc-ikvm and the client's KVM session is torn down.
+            // Swallow it and treat it as "no resize" so the daemon survives
+            // and keeps serving (a stale/no-signal frame) until the signal
+            // returns.
+            lg2::error("Video needsResize failed {ERROR}", "ERROR", e.what());
+            resizeNeeded = false;
+        }
+
+        if (resizeNeeded)
         {
             waitServer(true);
-            video.resize();
-            server.resize();
+            try
+            {
+                video.resize();
+                server.resize();
+            }
+            catch (const std::exception& e)
+            {
+                lg2::error("Video resize failed {ERROR}", "ERROR", e.what());
+            }
             setVideoDone();
         }
         else
